    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: address normalization on owner creation\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `OwnerAddress.java` (in `rest/function/owner/`, matching the existing `TelephoneE164`/`OwnerEmail` pattern). Its `normalize(String)`:\n- trims and collapses all internal whitespace runs to a single space,\n- upper-cases,\n- expands whole-word abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE` (token-matched so it won't corrupt substrings),\n- returns `\"\"` for null/blank input.\n\n**Wiring** (all in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline):\n- `ValidateNewOwner` \u2014 normalizes the address and writes it back on the request *before* the required-field check, so the blank check now rejects an address that is blank **after normalization** (400). The normalized value then flows through `BuildOwner` \u2192 mapper \u2192 `Owner`, so it's stored and returned.\n- `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` \u2014 the address side of the duplicate-household comparison now uses `OwnerAddress.normalize` on both the request and each existing owner.\n- `AssignHousehold` \u2014 the same normalized form is used both for matching same-household owners and for deriving the deterministic shared `householdId`.\n\nJavadoc on the three touched functions was updated to describe the new behaviour.\n\n**Tests:** the three new acceptance cases pass \u2014 `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`, and `\"   \"` \u2192 400 \u2014 and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` with no regressions.",
